  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "fairly-adv",
      "quite-adv",
      "rather-adv",
      "pretty-adv"
    ],
    "note": "All four mean *more than a little*. **Fairly** is the weakest and the most neutral: *fairly good*. **Pretty** is informal and a little stronger: *pretty good*. **Quite** is stronger in American English (*quite good* can mean *very good*) but often only *fairly* in British English. **Rather** often suggests that something is more than you expected or wanted: *rather cold*."
  },
